## Output Format: Edit Hunks

Output ONLY edit hunks in the format below. Do NOT output the full file.
Each hunk replaces one specific section of the existing file.

<<<EDIT_HUNK 1/N>>>
<<<OLD>>>
[exact verbatim text from the "Previous attempt" section in Requirements — must match character-for-character including all whitespace and newlines]
<<<NEW>>>
[replacement text that fixes the issue]
<<<END_HUNK>>>

Replace N with the total number of hunks in your output.

Rules:
1. OLD text MUST be an exact verbatim copy from the "Previous attempt" file content shown in Requirements.
   It will be used for exact string matching — any whitespace difference will cause the patch to fail.
2. Focus ONLY on sections that need to change to fix the reported issues.
   Do NOT touch sections that are already correct.
3. You may output multiple hunks if multiple independent sections need fixing.
4. Each hunk must be for a non-overlapping section of the file.
5. If no changes are needed (the file is already correct), output exactly: NO_CHANGES_NEEDED
6. Do NOT output any explanation, markdown fences, or text outside the hunk blocks.

You MUST follow the artifact type specification below. The Bundle Contract above takes precedence
for parameter names, env var names, and data types.

